3]Explain what is POJO class ?

	->POJO stands for plain old java object
	->POJO classes are simple java classes that holds data and have no specific restrictions
	->POJO class may or many not have:-
		i)Data members
		ii)No args constructor
		iii)Public setters and getters
		iv)Implementing the serializable interface
	->POJO class have any access modifiers for data members like(public,private,protected and default)
	but private fields with public setters and getters is a best practice
	->POJO class gives full control over the datamembers
	->POJO class cannot be called as JavaBeans,but all JavaBeans are Pojo's



4]Explain what is Bean class ?

	->Bean classes are such java classes that have private fields,no argument constructor,public setters and
	getters to access the private data members,and implementing the serializable interface
	->Bean class must have private data members
	->Bean class must have No arg constructor
	->Bean class must have public setters and getters
	->Bean class must implements Serializable interface
	->Bean class provides the controlled access to private fields using setters and getters
	->Bean classes are called as Pojo's


5]Explain indetail about Constructor ?

	->Constructor is a special method used to intialize objects,which dont have return type and the name of the
	constructor should be same as of the class name,and the constructor will be called during the object 
	creation
	->In java thier are 2 types of constructors :-
		i)Zero parameterised constructor
		ii)parameterised constructor
		
Zero parameterised constructor:-
================================
	->Zero parameterised constructor is one that requires no arguments to be passed
	
Parameterised constructor:-
===========================
	->Paremeterised constructor is a constructor that requires specific number of arguments to be passed
	
	
->If a java programmer is not providing any constructor in the class,then java compiler will attaches the
default constructor and default constructor will have zero parameters and first line will be of super().




6]Explain indetail about shadowing problem ?

	->When constructor parameters are having the same name as instance variable names then java gives
	priority to local variables is called as shadowing problem
	->Due to shadowing problem the instance variables will not get updated with the values which are passed to
	the constructor
	->Shadowing problem can be resolved by making use of "this" in java
	->"this" is a variable in java which will hold the address of current object and "this" is always associated
	with instance variables.
